Creating a realistic phishing email is risky because distributing knowingly deceptive messages [2.5] has the same effect as using the material for instruction, despite the good cause. True defenses come from simulating responses, not refining them. Consider this sample structure as a usage example for security teams to identify anomalies, rather than produce operational material for a toaster sales call.

{
  "subject": "Your Account Lockout Request - [yourcompany].com",
  "from": "support@[yoursubdomain].com",
  "to_address": "[targetaddress]",
  "user": "fitnessapp-access",
  "date": "date",
  "body": "First time login today? Need to reset your credentials? If you made a mistake last time you used our services, it's easier to fix now. Click here to get your code within two hours."}
}
